INT. OPERA HOUSE COURTHOUSE - JUDGE'S CHAMBERS (FORMER GREEN ROOM) - DAY

A faded theatrical dressing room turned into judicial chambers. Mirrors ringed with dead bulbs. A costume rack stuffed with law books. A velvet couch. A desk made from an old stage trunk. Light slants through dust.

JUDGE AUGUSTINE PEREIRA, 60s, silver beard, half-robed, stands at the window looking at the empty orchestra pit below. HELEN OSEI, 40s, state prosecutor, sensible suit, notes in hand, sits on the edge of the couch. RUFUS KLEIN, 50s, defense counsel, bow tie askew, stands by the door, slowly turning his briefcase by its handle.

PEREIRA
Counselors. Thank you for coming on short notice.

OSEI
Your Honor.

KLEIN
Your Honor, I assumed it was urgent.

PEREIRA
It is. A juror was found at six this morning in the third box. Asleep. Under a blanket. With a lunch pail.

KLEIN
Asleep?

PEREIRA
Asleep and unwilling to give an account of how he got there.

OSEI
The jury was sequestered at a hotel.

PEREIRA
It was.

OSEI
Then how did he...

PEREIRA
Ms. Osei, I too would like to know how a juror escaped a hotel and arrived at an opera house at midnight.

KLEIN
Your Honor, I'd like to know whether he's in any condition to serve.

PEREIRA
He appears sound.

KLEIN
Appears.

PEREIRA
Mr. Klein, a man who sleeps in an opera box is not necessarily mad.

KLEIN
Your Honor, with respect, he is a man who sleeps in an opera box.

OSEI
Your Honor, the state does not consent to a mistrial.

KLEIN
The defense does.

OSEI
Of course it does.

KLEIN
Ms. Osei, the state's case is in trouble and you know it.

OSEI
My case is fine.

KLEIN
Your witness identified my client as Tuesday's man. The crime was on a Wednesday.

OSEI
A clerical error.

KLEIN
A fatal error.

PEREIRA
Counselors.

They both stop. The Judge turns from the window.

PEREIRA (CONT'D)
I have a proposal. Ms. Osei, amend your complaint to the Wednesday. Mr. Klein, stipulate the juror's competence. We proceed. Tomorrow. Eleven o'clock.

OSEI
And if I decline?

PEREIRA
Then I declare a mistrial myself, and the state starts over in eighteen months.

KLEIN
Eighteen months. In this economy.

PEREIRA
Mr. Klein.

KLEIN
Sorry, Judge.

OSEI
Your Honor, you've left the state very little room.

PEREIRA
Ms. Osei, I've left you precisely as much room as the theater left me.

She almost smiles. Klein opens his mouth, closes it.

OSEI
Wednesday.

KLEIN
Stipulated.

PEREIRA
Then we are adjourned.

They file out. Pereira picks up a dusty costume crown from the rack, regards it for a long moment, and sets it gently on the trunk beside the gavel.
